  "query_preview": "..\n(Tomorrow through Monday)\nIssued at 1025 AM CST Mon Nov 23 2026\n\nThe aforementioned storm system will continue to make its approach\nTuesday, with a southern track through North Texas expected.\nPrecipitation associated with this system should remain just south\nof the area, although it may be close. Will keep POPs just below\nmentionable Tuesday night as it makes its closest approach to\nsoutheast Oklahoma. The Tuesday cloud cover will lead to even\nlower temperatures during the daytime than those today, with highs\n10 to 15 degrees cooler than normal in many spots. \n\nA second storm system dropping out of Canada through the Plains\nlate Wednesday into Thanksgiving Day will bring an increase in \ncloud cover and northerly winds to mainly northeast Oklahoma into\nwestern Arkansas, with any precipitation associated with it most\nlikely to be well east of the forecast area. Thanksgiving Day\nlooks to be a chilly one, with widespread hard or killing freezes\nacross the area to start the day. Bundle up for any Thanksgiving \nmorning outdoor activities. \n\nBeyond Thanksgiving Day, a return to southerly winds Friday as\nsurface high pressure moves away will also bring near to above\nnormal temperatures back to the region. The warmer weather is\nforecast to continue through at least the first half of the\nweekend and likely the entire weekend. A low pressure system is\nfeatured in the Central to Southern Plains on most models either\nlate in the weekend or early next week that, depending on its\nlocation and track, may bring a front into the area, as featured\nin the latest ECMWF and UKMET.",
